; Kepler's problem with its variational equations: kepler-sv-fp64 and one
; tangent vector, stepped beside the state by the same program. The
; tangent is derived, never written (docs/LANGUAGE.md, "The variational
; equations"): each quotient's tangent is (dx - r dr3)/r3 and the root's
; dr2/(2 sqrt(r2)), so a vector adds a run-time division for each
; division and root the step's tangent reads - three more routines a step
; (C4).
system kepler
format fp256
round  rne
state  x, y, px, py
tangent v
let r2 = fma(x, x, y * y)
let r3 = r2 * sqrt(r2)
d/dt x  = px
d/dt y  = py
d/dt px = -(x / r3)
d/dt py = -(y / r3)
step   stormer-verlet, h = 1/100, q = (x, y), p = (px, py)
